You know, Sofia, the journey to Potsdam is really beautiful.
The train rolled slowly out of Berlin.
We quickly left the houses behind us.
Then we drove through a dense pine forest.
I looked out of the window and only saw trees.
On the train I watched the other passengers.
At one station, many hikers got in.
They wore big hiking boots.
And they put their rucksacks on the floor.
A family also came into our carriage.
They travelled with three children.
The children ran very noisily through the carriage.
They laughed and played together.
The parents followed quickly behind.
I looked at the family and smiled.
Then I just stayed quietly in my seat.
The train drove further through the forest towards Potsdam.
